      "text": "To find the range, we need to consider the different cases where the signs of the expressions inside the absolute value functions change. This will correspond to the x-values where the expressions change from positive to negative or negative to positive.\nCase 1: $x+1>0$ and $x-1>0$\nIn this case, $|x+1| = x+1$ and $|x-1| = x-1$. So,\n$$G(x) = (x+1) - (x-1) = 2.$$\nCase 2: $x+1>0$ and $x-1<0$\nIn this case, $|x+1| = x+1$ and $|x-1| = -(x-1)$. So,\n$$G(x) = (x+1) - (-x+1) = 2x.$$\nSo, $G(x) = 2$ or $G(x) = 2x$ depending on the value of $x$.\nCase 3: $x+1<0$ and $x-1>0$\nIn this case, $|x+1| = -(x+1)$ and $|x-1| = x-1$. So,\n$$G(x) = -(x+1) - (x-1) = -2x.$$\nSo, $G(x) = -2x$ depending on the value of $x$.\nCase 4: $x+1<0$ and $x-1<0$\nIn this case, $|x+1| = -(x+1)$ and $|x-1| = -(x-1)$. So,\n$$G(x) = -(x+1) - (-x+1) = -2.$$\nSo, $G(x) = -2$.\nCombining all of these cases, we get $G(x) \\in \\boxed{\\{-2, 0, 2\\}}$.",
