      "text": "We can start by analyzing the function for different intervals of $x$.\n\n* If $x\\leq-1$, then $|x+1|$ = $-(x+1)$ and $|x-1|$ = $-(x-1)$, so $G(x)$ = $-(x+1)-(x-1)$ = $-2x$.\n\n* If $-1<x\\leq1$, then $|x+1|$ = $x+1$ and $|x-1|$ = $(x-1)$, so $G(x)$ = $(x+1)-(x-1)$ = $2$.\n\n* If $x>1$, then $|x+1|$ = $x+1$ and $|x-1|$ = $x-1$, so $G(x)$ = $x+1-(x-1)$ = $2$.\n\nThus, the function $G(x)$ takes on the values $-2x$ for $x\\leq-1$, the value $2$ for $-1<x\\leq1$, and the value $2$ for $x>1$. The range of $G(x)$ is all these values, or $(-\\infty, 2]\\cup \\{2\\}$.\n\nTherefore, the range of the function $G(x)$ is \\boxed{(-\\infty, 2]\\cup \\{2\\}}. The answer is: (-\\infty,2]\\cup\\{2\\}",
